WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.269
-The Republican Party has
decided that its path

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.505
back to power is complete and
total fealty to Donald Trump,

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:09.241
and they're purging anyone
who refuses to repeat his lies

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:10.443
about the 2020 election,

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.712
no matter how destructive
it is for the country.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.047
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:18.951 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:21.520
It is exceedingly rare
in the history of this country

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.856
for a political party
to stay so closely tied

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.257
to an ex-president,

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:27.826
let alone one who is as deeply
unpopular as Donald Trump.

00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:30.363
What we're seeing right now
in the Republican Party

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:32.598
is not usually how
the process unfolds

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:35.467
after a party loses power,
especially in a landslide,

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.504
amid a once-in-a-century
cataclysm.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:39.472
And let's remember,
the GOP didn't just lose,

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.307
they got wiped out.
They lost the presidency

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:42.708
and both houses of Congress.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:45.111
Trump never once cracked
50 percent job approval

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.579
and never won
the popular vote.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.282
Meanwhile, President Biden is
riding high with a 63 percent

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.417
approval ratings
in a new poll out today.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.486
The GOP is treating Trump
like a good luck charm

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:56.155
even after he brought
them terrible luck.

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.823
If the first time Dumbo
tried to fly,

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:59.992
he plummeted to the ground
and broke all four legs

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:03.195
and both ears, he would have let
go of the feather.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:05.665
And yet the GOP is still fully
enthralled to Trump,

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:08.301
who oversaw the worst economic
crash and unemployment crisis

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.970
in a century,
rising poverty and child hunger,

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.772
and a disastrous
pandemic response

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.641
that left hundreds of thousands
of Americans dead.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.410
Not to mention that violent
insurrection where he incited

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.312
a mountain of rioters
to ransack the Capitol

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.247
and disrupt the lawful
counting of electoral votes.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.882
You remember that?
Somehow it feels like it

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.383
was approximately
800 years ago

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.419
when in reality
it happened in January.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.120
Now Trump's shuffling
around his golf course

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.855
like it never happened,
popping up in photos

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.392
like a retired bigfoot
and interrupting weddings

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.326
and other private events
to drone on

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:35.561
about his deranged belief

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.029
that he actually
won the election.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:40.199
-The former president himself
is still waxing poetic

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.768
about finding irregularities
right around the corner,

00:01:42.768 --> 00:01:44.770
apparently living
in an alternate reality

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.072
down at Mar-a-Lago.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.408
-Watch Arizona,
some very interesting things

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.777
are happening in Arizona, right?
You know about that.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.547
And we just had a great ruling
or actually the Senate

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.115
the State Senate of Arizona.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.417
Let's see what they find,
I wouldn't be surprised

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.253
if they found thousands

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:02.388
and thousands
and thousands of votes.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.156
So we're going to watch
that very closely.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.792
And after that you'll watch
Pennsylvania

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.195
you'll watch Georgia,
and you're going to watch

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.365
Michigan and Wisconsin.
We get 75 million votes.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.401
Nobody's ever gotten that.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.470
They said,
"Get 66 million votes, sir.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.906
And the election's over," well,
I got 75 million.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.376
And they said --
well, you saw what happened.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.578
10:30 in the evening
all of a sudden they said

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.846
"That's a strange thing.

00:02:27.846 --> 00:02:30.850
Why are they closing up
certain place?"

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.451
A lot of things
happening right now.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:35.155
I just want to say
it's an honor to be here.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.256
It's an honor to have you
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.726
You are a great
and beautiful couple.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.761
-In fairness to Trump,
it's very hard

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.563
to do stand up comedy
when you're opening for a band.

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:47.267
I mean, he's just going
from room to room at Mar-a-Lago,

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.867
interrupting the most
sacred moments

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:51.170
in people's lives to whine
about his election loss.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.172
Like Bill Murray
with a head injury.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.573
[ As Trump ] You're going to
find thousands of votes

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:57.677
in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin,
Arizona. A lot of things are

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.079
happening with the mail ballots
and the signature matches.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.548
I said you got
to get the signatures.

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.016
And they say,
"Sir, we can't, sir."

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:07.086
And I say "That's. That's a
strange thing, isn't it?

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.890
Anyway, enjoy the bris.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.925
Let me know if you need a mohel.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:19.031
I got a guy so good, so good.
He also cuts Rudy's hair."

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.265
[ Normal voice ]
Although I'm guessing

00:03:20.265 --> 00:03:22.401
if you hold a wedding reception
at Mar-a-Lago

00:03:22.401 --> 00:03:25.271
at this point, you're counting
on Trump popping in.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.373
It's like having a birthday
party at Chuck E. Cheese.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.610
The rat better be there or
there's going to be hell to pay.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.278
"What do you mean
it's Chuck's days off?"

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.046
"Well, technically,
he's in the shop

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:35.481
because he had
a mechanical error

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.550
that made it look like he was
giving kids a middle finger.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.251
But they like tell him
he has the day off."

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.020
"what am I supposed to tell
my son whose birthday it is

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.888
and he was dying to meet
Chuck E. Cheese?"

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:45.891
"You could tell him
Jasper T. Jowls is still here."

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:49.629
"Nobody likes Jasper T. Jowls!"

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:52.097
"Also, sometimes Donald Trump
rolls through and complains

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:54.667
about Brad Raffensperger."

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.002
And by the way,
that insane Arizona audit

00:03:57.002 --> 00:03:59.572
he referenced is the same one
you may have heard where

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:03.209
Republicans are reportedly
searching for bamboo on ballots

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.078
to find out if they were
smuggled in from Asia.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.379
-The other day
at the press conference,

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.348
you were talking about bamboo.
What was that about?

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.552
-Well, is that there's
accusations of 40,000 ballots

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.186
were flown in.
-To Arizona?

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:17.757
-To Arizona, and it was stuffed
into the box, okay?

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:22.661
And it came from the southeast
part of the world, Asia, okay.

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:26.131
And and what they're doing
is to find out

00:04:26.131 --> 00:04:29.768
if there's bamboo in the paper.
That camera right there

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.837
that they take a picture
of the ballot.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:35.608
If you -- they can really
look at depth and find out,

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:39.912
is it a hand-marked paper ballot
because it's a 5k camera.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.146
-And why do you check for
bamboo?

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:44.116
-Because they use bamboo
in their paper processing,

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:47.753
-Who's they?
-People in Southeast Asia.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.755
-They're using a 5k camera
to find out

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.056
if there's bamboo in the paper

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:52.992
to see if the ballots
came from Southeast Asia.

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:56.061
Imagine going to Best Buy to
get the camera and explaining.

00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:57.829
That's what it's for.

00:04:57.829 --> 00:04:59.632
"Are you looking for something
for your family photos

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.000
or something more professional?"
"Well, I'm looking for something

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.104
that can detect strands
of bamboo on ballots.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.673
Why are you calling
store security?

00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:09.175
Is that bamboo
in your shirt?

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.576
Guys? They're on to me.
Oh, damn it.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.579
Um, do you also have those,
like, secret wrist microphones?"

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.548
Also, what a waste
of a 5k camera.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.015
This is an actual
television show,

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:19.652
and I'm pretty sure we have,
at best, 1.5k's.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:23.289
I don't even know what the "K"
in 5k stands for.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.623
I tried to find out,
but whenever I asked,

00:05:24.623 --> 00:05:26.258
my crew tells me it stands for

00:05:26.258 --> 00:05:28.861
"It's none of your [Bleep]
business, 'kay."

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.563
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:32.931
When I was in my attic
during quarantine,

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:35.768
I had to film myself
on my own iPad

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:38.571
because NBC refused to send
actual TV cameras to my house.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.240
They said a 5k camera
would be wasted

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.708
on bits about "The Thornburgs,"

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:44.810
a magic door,
and the wasps I befriended.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.579
And they definitely
did not like the sea captain.

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.914
The programing execs sat me down
and said to me,

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:52.218
And this is true, "Why won't the
sea captain work for a dolphin?"

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.386
And I said, "Why?"

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.687
And they said,
"Because he serves no porpoise."

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.456
[ Laughs ]

00:05:57.456 --> 00:06:01.994
Who let the sea captain
write a joke?

00:06:01.994 --> 00:06:05.664
For real. In May?

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:06.933
By the way,
just to clarify,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.668
the guy who explained
that whole insane

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.404
bamboo ballot theory
doesn't believe it.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.172
As he explained later
in the interview.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.241
-So that you feel like --
-That's what they say.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:18.344
-40,000 ballots have been--?

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.212
-Yeah, I don't believe
any of that.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:23.749
I'm just saying that is
part of the mystery

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:27.253
that we want to un-gaslight
like people about.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:28.654
And this is a way to do it.
-This part of

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.790
what you're looking at for it.
-I'm not. They are.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.858
-Poor guy.
These people are so crazy

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:35.494
that if you explain
what they believe,

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:39.064
people think you are crazy.
They're crazy, is airborne.

00:06:39.064 --> 00:06:41.300
For some reason, it fell to him
to explain to the press

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.768
what these people
are looking for.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.037
It's like coming home from work
and trying to calmly explain

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.438
to your wife
that you're late for dinner

00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:48.941
because the guy in the F train
pulled the emergency brake

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.110
because he thought a cockroach
stole his cigarette.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.078
So he claimed, and again,
these are his words,

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.347
a cockroach came up to him

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:56.615
and asked him for directions
to the nearest OTB.

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:58.551
And while he was looking,
again his words,

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:00.519
the cockroach reached
into his pocket

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:01.987
and stole his Marlboro Light.

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:03.555
I don't know.
That's what he said.

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:05.658
[ Deep voice ] Sorry.
It's a true story.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:07.659
I just needed a smoke.
I'm a little stressed out.

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:11.230
The Mets can't hit with runners
in scoring position.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:15.467
This cigarette tastes weird,
is this bamboo?

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:20.205
Does anyone on the train
have that 5k camera?

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:21.641
[ Normal voice ]
Anyway, the point is,

00:07:21.641 --> 00:07:23.910
this is what the Republican
Party has committed itself to.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.612
Most political parties
would move on and engage

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:29.515
in some level of introspection
and self assessment

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.884
after being repeatedly rejected
by a majority of voters

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:33.386
and losing power entirely.

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.954
They'd also move on
from a president

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:38.090
who was both deeply unpopular
and left the nation in ruins.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.792
Instead, Republicans are
intensifying

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.059
their devotion to Trump.

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:42.628
They're in the process
right now, pushing

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:45.498
Wyoming Congressman Liz Cheney
out of a leadership role

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:48.367
simply because she affirmed
the basic reality --

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.702
Trump lost the election --

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:51.470
and called the idea
that it was stolen from him

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.239
a toxic lie
that undermines democracy.

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:54.873
And again,
as I've said many times now,

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.508
I did not want to side
with Liz Cheney.

00:07:56.508 --> 00:07:57.542
She's not a hero.

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.111
She's a pro-war
torture apologist

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:01.180
who stood by Trump in 2016

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.482
and during his first
impeachment trial

00:08:03.482 --> 00:08:06.418
and helped build the modern GOP
into what it is today.

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:08.888
She's as much to blame
for the rise of Trump-ism

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:10.622
as anyone else
in Republican leadership.

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:12.391
I don't want to support her
any more than I want to

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:14.393
hang out with Jasper T. Jowls.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.428
It's just that now
she's being purged

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:18.864
for simply stating the reality
that Trump lost

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:20.399
and there was
no widespread fraud.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.101
And now Republicans
want to replace her

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:24.670
with New York Congresswoman
Elise Stefanik,

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.205
a Trump loyalist
who has repeated

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:27.339
his debunked election lies

00:08:27.339 --> 00:08:29.608
and said last week
on Steve Bannon's podcast

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:32.545
that she supports the
nutty Arizona election audit.

00:08:32.545 --> 00:08:35.948
-What are your thoughts about
what's going on in Arizona?

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:38.917
-I fully support
the audit in Arizona.

00:08:38.917 --> 00:08:42.822
-We want transparency and
answers for the American people.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:45.991
What are the Democrats
so afraid of?

00:08:45.991 --> 00:08:49.561
The voters in Arizona
and the state Senate in Arizona

00:08:49.561 --> 00:08:52.164
pursued this audit.
I fully support it.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.266
Transparency is a good thing.

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:57.502
We need to fix these election
security issues

00:08:57.502 --> 00:08:59.104
going into the future.

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:02.474
-What election security issues?
Strands of bamboo on ballots

00:09:02.474 --> 00:09:04.310
smuggled in from Asia.
What's next?

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.645
We're also using a 5k camera

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:08.580
to look for microscopic
marinara stains

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.150
to make sure no ballots were
secretly smuggled in from Italy?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.754
I personally witnessed
an Antifa fraudster

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:16.988
sneak into the counting room
with a calzone

00:09:16.988 --> 00:09:20.092
stuffed with pepperoni
and fraudulent ballots.

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.493
This is all that matters
in today's GOP.

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:23.462
Your willingness to repeat
Trump's deranged

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.598
lies about the election
and codify them

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:27.600
into law
through voter suppression bills

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.401
that will let Republicans
steal the next election.

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:31.036
That's why Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis

00:09:31.036 --> 00:09:33.906
was on "Fox News" last week
signing a voter suppression bill

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:35.875
surrounded by fawning
Trump fans.

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:38.443
Over the weekend,
GOP Congressman Jim Banks

00:09:38.443 --> 00:09:41.112
said he supported Cheney's
ouster and essentially accused

00:09:41.112 --> 00:09:44.250
her of abandoning Republicans
by acknowledging reality.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:48.220
-Do you still question
whether or not Joe Biden

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:50.956
won the election fair
and square

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:57.729
and got over 270 electoral votes
fair and square?

00:09:57.729 --> 00:10:01.467
-Yeah, Chris, I stand by my vote
to object on January 6th.

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:04.870
I stand by the Texas lawsuit
because I have serious concerns

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:08.607
about how the election
in November was was carried out.

00:10:08.607 --> 00:10:11.610
-When Liz Cheney says history
is watching

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:15.414
and you can't go forward
until you resolve this question.

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:16.983
The election
was fair and square.

00:10:16.983 --> 00:10:22.188
Donald Trump
played a negative role.

00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:26.125
You think she's misguided
making those points?

00:10:26.125 --> 00:10:29.895
-Yeah. I've called on Liz Cheney
to rejoin the Republican team

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:31.763
and help us go out
and win the majority

00:10:31.763 --> 00:10:33.299
in the midterm election.

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:34.967
-"I've called Liz Cheney
to rejoin

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:36.635
the Republican team
to acknowledge

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:38.637
that there are serious
concerns about the election

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:41.173
and to admit that we are,
in fact, living in The Matrix.

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:44.209
That's why I'm supporting
as her replacement Morpheus,

00:10:44.209 --> 00:10:45.544
who has made
some very persuasive

00:10:45.544 --> 00:10:49.348
points about voter fraud.
And he knows kung fu.

00:10:49.348 --> 00:10:51.583
Learned it in a day."
But listen to what he said,

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:53.251
that's actually a fairly
shocking admission.

00:10:53.251 --> 00:10:54.853
He essentially said Cheney
is abandoning

00:10:54.853 --> 00:10:56.422
Republicans
by acknowledging reality.

00:10:56.422 --> 00:10:58.290
Meaning that there
are two separate things.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.658
Republicans don't
live in reality.

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:02.661
In fact, in order to be a member
of this Republican Party,

00:11:02.661 --> 00:11:03.796
you have to abandon reality.

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:05.430
It's like insisting
to your children

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.932
that the guy
in the Mickey Mouse costume

00:11:06.932 --> 00:11:08.833
is the actual Mickey Mouse.

00:11:08.833 --> 00:11:11.203
Even though your kids
are now thirty five years old,

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:12.871
"You can either
rejoin this family

00:11:12.871 --> 00:11:15.207
on our annual trip to
Typhoon Lagoon and acknowledge

00:11:15.207 --> 00:11:17.009
that Mickey Mouse
is a real person.

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:18.510
Or you can get
the hell out of here.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.913
And are you smoking another
one of those bamboo cigarettes?

00:11:20.913 --> 00:11:22.847
Did you steal that
from a cockroach?"

00:11:22.847 --> 00:11:25.951
[ Deep voice ] Guilty.

00:11:25.951 --> 00:11:30.489
[ Normal voice ]
Is that as popular a recurring
character that we think it is?

00:11:30.489 --> 00:11:32.724
Cigarette smoking cockroach?

00:11:32.724 --> 00:11:34.426
We'll find out
on the old comments.

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:36.461
[ Laughter ]

00:11:36.461 --> 00:11:38.731
And even, by the way,
we did a full clip

00:11:38.731 --> 00:11:42.134
about Donald Trump
crashing weddings.

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:43.835
No Vince Vaughn.

00:11:43.835 --> 00:11:47.139
That's restraint.

00:11:47.139 --> 00:11:49.074
And even Republicans
who are no longer in office,

00:11:49.074 --> 00:11:51.276
like Chris Christie, are blaming
Cheney for her choice

00:11:51.276 --> 00:11:52.610
to simply live in reality

00:11:52.610 --> 00:11:54.780
rather than Republicans
for lying about the election

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.081
and dismantling democracy.

00:11:56.081 --> 00:11:58.150
-I think Liz is doing
what she wants to do.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.252
I don't think Liz wants to
be in leadership anymore,

00:12:00.252 --> 00:12:03.022
because once she won
the vote earlier,

00:12:03.022 --> 00:12:05.391
she continued to press
this issue publicly

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:08.828
in a way that was antagonizing
the people who were against her.

00:12:08.828 --> 00:12:11.630
And I think you don't have an
entitlement to be in leadership.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.065
-Think about how sad it is

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:14.900
to still be loyal
to a guy like Trump

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.501
after everything he put
Chris Christie through,

00:12:16.501 --> 00:12:19.572
among all the other humiliations
Christie suffered.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:21.840
Trump once forced him to eat
meat loaf at the White House,

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:25.377
a place where they famously will
literally make anything for you.

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:26.578
"Mr. Christie,
before you order,

00:12:26.578 --> 00:12:28.447
we have the most exquisite
culinary creations

00:12:28.447 --> 00:12:29.581
you can imagine
from a chef

00:12:29.581 --> 00:12:30.982
who lives here
on the premises."

00:12:30.982 --> 00:12:32.952
[ As Trump ] He'll have the
meatloaf.

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.320
Bring him a side of ketchup.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.721
And Christie is
still sticking by Trump.

00:12:35.721 --> 00:12:37.089
Maybe that's what
you have to do

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:38.623
to keep your job
in this Republican Party.

00:12:38.623 --> 00:12:40.192
In order to demonstrate
your fealty to Trump,

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:41.827
you have to lie
about the election

00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:43.929
and eat a giant plate
of meatloaf on TV

00:12:43.929 --> 00:12:45.497
while he insults your wife
and your dad

00:12:45.497 --> 00:12:47.666
and then, for good measure,
kicks you in the balls.

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:49.067
[ As Giuliani ] Don't worry,
boss, I'm wearing a cup.

00:12:49.067 --> 00:12:51.136
It's great
because it doubles as a mask.

00:12:51.136 --> 00:12:54.106
[ Normal voice ]
Any sane political party
would move on from a president

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:55.474
who is both deeply unpopular,

00:12:55.474 --> 00:12:58.209
lost by a wide margin,
and, on top of everything else,

00:12:58.209 --> 00:13:00.312
left nothing but misery
and destruction in his wake.

00:13:00.312 --> 00:13:02.247
And yet, Republicans
are not moving on.

00:13:02.247 --> 00:13:03.382
They're doubling down.

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:04.850
There as committed
to Trump as ever,

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.519
and now they don't care much
about how they have to lie

00:13:07.519 --> 00:13:09.521
or debase themselves
to prove their loyalty to him.

00:13:09.521 --> 00:13:11.590
Republicans are looking
at Trump's election lies

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:13.625
in their own voter suppression
bills and saying --

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:16.328
-You are a
great and beautiful couple.

00:13:16.328 --> 00:13:17.896
-This has been A Closer Look.

